["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Ducks leave little sign on the land. Their best sign is in the air: where they fly at first and last light.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A duck pond with five numbered clues, tips. 1: droppings on logs and beaver dams. 2: feathers at the water edge. 3: muddy, stirred up water where ducks tipped up to feed. 4: open lanes swum through duckweed. 5: webbed tracks in the mud.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sign on a duck pond: five clues</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"120\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".55\"/><path d=\"M0 160 Q100 150 200 164 T400 158 L400 300 L0 300Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"150\" width=\"110\" height=\"14\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"148\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#e9e2d0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><ellipse cx=\"90\" cy=\"146\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#e9e2d0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><ellipse cx=\"120\" cy=\"149\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#e9e2d0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M220 172 q6 -8 12 -2 q-4 6 -12 2Z\" fill=\"#f4f1e6\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M234 168 q6 -8 12 -2 q-4 6 -12 2Z\" fill=\"#f4f1e6\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M250 175 q6 -8 12 -2 q-4 6 -12 2Z\" fill=\"#f4f1e6\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"100\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a7a5a\" opacity=\".6\"/><path d=\"M150 70 Q200 90 260 70\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"10\" fill=\"none\" opacity=\".5\"/><g transform=\"translate(330 230) scale(0.4)\"><path d=\"M0 0 L-26 -40 Q-14 -34 0 -48 Q14 -34 26 -40 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".35\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-26\" y2=\"-40\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"-50\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"26\" y2=\"-40\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-4\" y2=\"10\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(352 214) scale(0.4)\"><path d=\"M0 0 L-26 -40 Q-14 -34 0 -48 Q14 -34 26 -40 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".35\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-26\" y2=\"-40\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"-50\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"26\" y2=\"-40\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-4\" y2=\"10\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(372 236) scale(0.4)\"><path d=\"M0 0 L-26 -40 Q-14 -34 0 -48 Q14 -34 26 -40 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".35\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-26\" y2=\"-40\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"-50\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"26\" y2=\"-40\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-4\" y2=\"10\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"/></g><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"136\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"95\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><circle cx=\"236\" cy=\"194\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"236\" y=\"199\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"82\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"87\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><circle cx=\"204\" cy=\"64\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"204\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><circle cx=\"352\" cy=\"270\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"352\" y=\"275\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">1 Droppings on logs</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">2 Feathers at the edge</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">3 Muddy, stirred water</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">4 Lanes in duckweed</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">5 Webbed tracks in mud</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Five pond clues: droppings, feathers, muddy water, lanes, tracks (Tip).</li><li>Many clues, fresh: ducks use it now (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: reading a pond</summary><ul><li>Droppings on logs, rocks and beaver dams where ducks loaf (Tip).</li><li>Feathers along the edge, most in late summer and early fall when birds moult (Tip).</li><li>Muddy, stirred water in the shallows where puddle ducks tipped up (Tip).</li><li>Open lanes swum through duckweed or floating leaves (Tip).</li><li>Webbed tracks in soft mud at the edge <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>The best proof is still your eyes: ducks on the water at first or last light (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Tracks on a 1 centimetre grid. Left, a duck: three forward toes joined by webbing and a tiny hind toe, about 6 centimetres long for a mallard, 60 percent. Right, a coot: long toes with separate lobes and no web. A goose track has the same shape as a duck but is much bigger, 75 percent.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Webbed track, to scale (1 cm grid)</text><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"10\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"230\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"270\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"290\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"310\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"350\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"350\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"370\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"390\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"160\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e3e3d3\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><g transform=\"translate(80 170) scale(1.2)\"><path d=\"M0 0 L-26 -40 Q-14 -34 0 -48 Q14 -34 26 -40 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".35\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-26\" y2=\"-40\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"-50\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"26\" y2=\"-40\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-4\" y2=\"10\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"/></g><text x=\"80\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Duck: 3 toes webbed</text><line x1=\"42\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"112\" y2=\"196\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"78\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">about 6 cm</text><g transform=\"translate(300 175) scale(1.2)\"><ellipse cx=\"-15.0\" cy=\"-22.0\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"20.0\" transform=\"rotate(-27.0 -15.0 -22.0)\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".5\"/><ellipse cx=\"0.0\" cy=\"-28.0\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"25.454545454545453\" transform=\"rotate(0.0 0.0 -28.0)\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".5\"/><ellipse cx=\"15.0\" cy=\"-22.0\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"20.0\" transform=\"rotate(27.0 15.0 -22.0)\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".5\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-30\" y2=\"-44\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"-56\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"-44\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-6\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/></g><text x=\"300\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Coot: lobed, no web</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"254\" width=\"380\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Goose: same shape, much bigger (75%)</text></svg>\n</figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-duck-tracks.jpg\" alt=\"Webbed tracks in mud: 3 forward toes joined by skin.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Webbed tracks in mud: 3 forward toes joined by skin. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Ryan Hodnett, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anatidae_Footprints_-_Guelph,_Ontario_2020-04-12.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Three toes forward, joined by web, a tiny hind toe <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>A mallard track is about 6 cm long <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: tracks in detail</summary><ul><li>Duck feet: three forward toes joined by webbing, and a short hind toe that often barely prints <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>A small sample of fresh mallard tracks in silt averaged about 62 mm long and 66 mm wide (60%, one source, 4 tracks).</li><li>Goose and gull tracks look like duck tracks; geese are much bigger <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Coots have long toes with lobes, not a full web <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Lots of overlapping tracks at one spot of shore: a loafing or feeding spot (Tip).</li><li>More on reading tracks: <a href=\"#/s/tracks\">Tracks</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Sign</th><th>What it means (Tip)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fresh droppings on a log</td><td>Birds loafed here today or yesterday</td></tr><tr><td>Muddy water in the shallows</td><td>Puddle ducks fed here recently</td></tr><tr><td>Lanes through duckweed</td><td>Birds swam here; fresh lanes close fast</td></tr><tr><td>Grain spilled by a field pond</td><td>Mallards may feed here at dawn</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Fresh is wet and shiny; old is dry and white (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to age sign (opinion)</summary><ul><li>Droppings: wet and dark green or brown is fresh; dry, crusted and white is old (Tip).</li><li>Muddy water settles within hours on a calm pond, so muddy water means birds were there very recently (Tip).</li><li>Duckweed lanes close up within a day (Tip).</li><li>These are field judgements, not measured rates. Confirm with a dawn or dusk watch (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three kinds of feather. A wing feather: stiff and long with a strong quill, sometimes with a coloured patch. A body feather: curved and soft. Down: fluff. A coloured wing feather can name the duck, 80 percent. A pile of plucked feathers is a predator kill, a tip.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Three kinds of feather, three stories</text><path d=\"M70 190 Q52 120.0 70 50 Q88 120.0 70 190Z\" fill=\"#5c5c5c\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"54\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><rect x=\"62\" y=\"120\" width=\"16\" height=\"30\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#3f51a0\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wing feather</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stiff, long</text><path d=\"M200 190 Q178 155.0 200 120 Q222 155.0 200 190Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Body feather</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">curved, soft</text><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"360.0\" y2=\"170.0\" stroke=\"#9a9a8a\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"354.24082524936455\" y2=\"187.67434273826808\" stroke=\"#9a9a8a\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"339.1745072513487\" y2=\"198.56271024771547\" stroke=\"#9a9a8a\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"320.58568321923354\" y2=\"198.48456844593892\" stroke=\"#9a9a8a\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"305.6114388870033\" y2=\"187.46991948572247\" stroke=\"#9a9a8a\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"300.0010602458597\" y2=\"169.74778257898555\" stroke=\"#9a9a8a\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"305.9086240299081\" y2=\"152.12248328576706\" stroke=\"#9a9a8a\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"321.065950760291\" y2=\"141.3611668501935\" stroke=\"#9a9a8a\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"339.6534608774917\" y2=\"141.59558673222173\" stroke=\"#9a9a8a\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"354.53457311856585\" y2=\"152.73573859414347\" stroke=\"#9a9a8a\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"170\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#bdbdad\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Down</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">fluff</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"48\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Coloured wing feather: names the duck (80%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pile of plucked feathers: a predator kill (Tip)</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A coloured wing feather names the duck <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Down and body feathers in late summer: a moult spot (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: feathers in detail</summary><ul><li>Wing feathers with the speculum colour tell the species <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Keep one for your ID kit.</li><li>Ducks drop all flight feathers at once in summer, so in July and August shore spots can be littered with feathers (85% for the moult, Tip for the litter).</li><li>A pile of plucked feathers and a few bones: an eagle, hawk or mink kill (Tip).</li><li>Feathers on the water at dawn after a calm night: birds roosted there (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"video\"><video controls preload=\"none\" playsinline src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a0/Mallards_%28Anas_platyrhynchos%29.webm/Mallards_%28Anas_platyrhynchos%29.webm.480p.vp9.webm\"></video><figcaption>Mallards up close: hear the hen and the drake. <span class=\"credit\">Video: The Nature Box, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mallards_(Anas_platyrhynchos).webm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a>. Needs internet.</span></figcaption></figure><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JlxfzLfnC7g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>How to Blow a Duck Call: The Basic Quack for Beginners</b><small>The basic quack, slowly.<br>Midwest Flyways, YouTube, 2 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a><ul><li>Loud quack: mallard hen. Soft raspy call: drake <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Whistles: wigeon, pintail, teal drakes <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: who says what</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Sound</th><th>Who (70 to 80%)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Loud, repeated quack</td><td>Mallard hen (the classic duck sound)</td></tr><tr><td>Soft, raspy \"rab rab\"</td><td>Mallard drake</td></tr><tr><td>Three note whistle</td><td>Wigeon drake</td></tr><tr><td>High \"peep\" or trill</td><td>Green winged teal drake</td></tr><tr><td>Soft whistle</td><td>Pintail drake</td></tr><tr><td>Whistling wings, no voice needed</td><td>Goldeneyes</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Listen at dawn from the truck or a high point before you walk in (Tip).</li><li>Mallard voices sit at 1 to 3 kHz, the band ducks hear best <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation. From far off, a hunter watches a roost lake at last light. A flock lifts off and flies along a line to a cut field, where they land. A flag marks the spot. End card: mark the spot and hunt it at dawn, a tip.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Scout: watch where they go at last light</text><ellipse cx=\"80\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"66\" ry=\"40\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Roost lake</text><rect x=\"268\" y=\"100\" width=\"124\" height=\"90\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#d9c27a\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cut field</text><path d=\"M190 250 L214 222 L238 250Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"214\" cy=\"226\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"214\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">You, far off</text><g><animateMotion dur=\"5s\" begin=\"0.0s\" fill=\"freeze\" path=\"M90 140 Q190 70 300 130\"/><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse rx=\"3\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"9;3;9\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"13\"/></ellipse></g><g><animateMotion dur=\"5s\" begin=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\" path=\"M90 140 Q190 70 314 138\"/><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse rx=\"3\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"9;3;9\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"13\"/></ellipse></g><g><animateMotion dur=\"5s\" begin=\"1.0s\" fill=\"freeze\" path=\"M90 140 Q190 70 328 146\"/><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse rx=\"3\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"9;3;9\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"13\"/></ellipse></g><g><animateMotion dur=\"5s\" begin=\"1.5s\" fill=\"freeze\" path=\"M90 140 Q190 70 342 154\"/><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse rx=\"3\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"9;3;9\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"13\"/></ellipse></g><g><animateMotion dur=\"5s\" begin=\"2.0s\" fill=\"freeze\" path=\"M90 140 Q190 70 356 162\"/><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse rx=\"3\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"9;3;9\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"13\"/></ellipse></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"5.6s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><path d=\"M330 120 l0 -26\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M330 94 l18 6 l-18 6Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.2s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"34\" width=\"380\" height=\"32\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mark the spot. Hunt it at dawn (Tip)</text></g></svg>\n<figcaption>Scout: watch where they go at last light. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Watch from far away; never walk in (Tip).</li><li>Mark where they land. Be there at dawn (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how an old hand scouts (opinion, widely taught)</summary><ul><li>Sit far off with binoculars at last light. Watch which way the birds leave the roost and where they drop (Tip).</li><li>Field hunting depends on finding the field they used yesterday (99% that permission is needed on private fields; the rest is Tip).</li><li>Watch two evenings if you can. Ducks often use the same field while the food lasts (Tip).</li><li>Do not drive or walk into the field to look closer. You will push them (Tip).</li><li>Mark it on the Hunt Map with a waypoint and the time (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Clue</th><th>Fresh</th><th>Old (Tip)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ducks seen</td><td>Last light yesterday</td><td>Last week</td></tr><tr><td>Droppings</td><td>Wet, shiny</td><td>Dry, white, crusted</td></tr><tr><td>Feathers</td><td>Clean, dry, fluffy</td><td>Wet, matted, dirty</td></tr><tr><td>Water</td><td>Muddy, stirred</td><td>Clear, settled</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Sign tells you \"maybe\". Birds in the air tell you \"yes\" (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why sign is weak for ducks</summary><ul><li>Ducks spend most of their time on water, where tracks do not last (Tip).</li><li>Pressure moves them fast: a pond full on Friday can be empty on Saturday (80% that pressure moves them, Tip for the timing).</li><li>Old hand's rule (opinion): \"Scout with your eyes, not your boots.\"</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a pond: shoot only where you can fetch. A shallow green zone near shore can be waded, so shooting is OK there. Deep water and a fast creek outlet are red: no shot. Mark each fall with a tree or rock behind it and go straight there.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"240\" width=\"400\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n  <path d=\"M20 240 C 20 120, 120 40, 220 40 C 330 40, 380 130, 380 240 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <path d=\"M40 240 C 50 180, 120 140, 200 140 C 280 140, 350 180, 360 240 Z\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\" opacity=\".35\"/>\n  <path d=\"M340 90 L400 60 L400 100 L360 120 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M360 96 l16 -6 m-4 -3 l4 3 l-4 4\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Shallow: wade it, OK</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Deep: no shot</text>\n  <text x=\"392\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"end\">fast water: no</text>\n  <rect x=\"170\" y=\"246\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"90,40 100,10 110,40\"/></g>\n  <circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"170\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M110 170 L100 44\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Mark the fall: tree behind it, walk straight</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Mark every fall against a tree or rock (Tip).</li><li>Cripples swim for the shore and cover. Check the bank <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: after the fall</summary><ul><li>Wounded ducks often dive and stay under longer with each dive <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Most cripples head for shore; check the edge cover <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>If a duck's head is still up, shoot again before you go after it (65%, dog trainer advice).</li><li>Mark all birds. If you cannot mark them all, shoot less <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Retrieval is the law: you must have a way to retrieve, and must make the effort <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds/21\">Rule Book</a>.</li><li>More in <a href=\"#/s/mc-ducks-10\">Masterclass 10</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Hook</th><th>Means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>\"Droppings, feathers, mud, lanes, tracks\"</td><td>5 pond clues (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>6 cm</td><td>Mallard track <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></td></tr><tr><td>\"Hen quacks, drake rasps\"</td><td>Mallard voices <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>\"Whistle on the water: wigeon or teal\"</td><td>Drake whistles <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td></tr><tr><td>\"Scout with your eyes, not your boots\"</td><td>Never walk in (Tip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Old hand's rule (opinion, widely taught): \"Hunt where they WANT to be tomorrow, not where they were last week.\"</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li>\"Head up, shoot again.\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li><li>\"Mark it on a tree.\" Every fall against a landmark (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Main source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tracks</td><td>Tracking references</td></tr><tr><td>Calls</td><td>Ducks Unlimited, Delta Waterfowl</td></tr><tr><td>Retrieval</td><td>Outdoor Life, Rule Book</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source, with date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.skullsite.co.uk/Prints/Mallard/mallard.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Skullsite, mallard prints</a>: 62 by 66 mm. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://wildwoodtracking.com/quiz/bbq17/bbquiz17A.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wildwood Tracking quiz</a>: webbed toes, stubby hind toe, geese bigger. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://bt.e-ditionsbyfry.com/article/Duck+Talk/3060494/495395/article.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, Duck talk</a> and <a href=\"https://deltawaterfowl.org/expand-your-vocabulary\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Delta Waterfowl, Expand your vocabulary</a>: who quacks and who whistles. Search preview 2026-10-11 (70 to 75%).</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.ca/assets/2021/10/waterfowl-ID-guide-2020-EN-reader-spreads.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited Canada ID guide</a>: mallard quack, wigeon whistle. Checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.outdoorlife.com/deep-dives/waterfowl-crippling-rates-hunting/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Life, waterfowl crippling rates</a>: cripples dive, head for shore, shoot again if the head is up, mark every bird. Read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Moult: see <a href=\"#/s/mc-ducks-05\">Masterclass 5</a> sources <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Retrieval law: app Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details>"]